      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. i just ran it through the internal tool and the term density score came back a bit lower than what the senior researchers usually expect for these briefs. it's a solid summary, but it might not hit the threshold for the high-level archive.\n\ncan you try an expanded version? go into even more detail about the molecular mechanisms—the lipids, the immunological pathways, etc. just please, i'm begging you, do NOT just stuff it with keywords to make the score go up. i need a deep-dive that actually makes sense to a biochemist. if it reads like a list of terms instead of a cohesive summary, it's a waste of time. \n\ntry to make it much more \"dense\" in terms of technical depth, but keep the scientific integrity 100% intact.",
